<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Greece and the Aegean</p><h1 class="st-title">Corinth</h1><p class="st-meta">900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.) · capital Corinth</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Wealthy trading city on the Isthmus, founder of Syracuse and Corcyra and a leading power of Archaic Greece, destroyed by Rome in 146 BCE.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Corinth grew in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> on the Isthmus linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> to central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, below the fortress hill of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acrocorinth">Acrocorinth</a>. Dorian settlers formed the city, and from the 8th century BCE it was governed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bacchiadae">Bacchiad</a> clan, who founded <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corcyra">Corcyra</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/syracuse">Syracuse</a> in 733 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cypselus">Cypselus</a> overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bacchiadae">Bacchiads</a> c. 657 BCE, and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/periander">Periander</a> made Corinth a major power. Corinthian pottery dominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> markets in the 7th century BCE, and the diolkos let ships be dragged across the Isthmus. After the tyranny an oligarchy ruled, and Corinth was a key ally in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/peloponnesian-league">Peloponnesian League</a>; its quarrels with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corcyra">Corcyra</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/athens">Athens</a> helped start the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Corinth fought <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sparta">Sparta</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corinthian-war">Corinthian War</a> of 395 to 387 BCE. Macedonian kings garrisoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acrocorinth">Acrocorinth</a> until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aratus-of-sicyon">Aratus</a> took it for the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/achaean-league">Achaean League</a> in 243 BCE. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucius-mummius-achaicus">Lucius Mummius</a> destroyed Corinth in 146 BCE; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> refounded it as a Roman colony in 44 BCE.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Greece and the Aegean</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:41.79%;width:15.00%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>900 BCE – 146 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/10th-century-bce">10th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Corinth</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cypselus, Periander</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Greek religion; cults of Poseidon and Aphrodite</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Doric Greek</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Korinthos</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-523&amp;focus=corinth" aria-label="Corinth on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5252 814 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Corinth lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5572 1070L5562 1098M5572 1070L5552 978M5572 1070L5549 1060M5572 1070L5304 942M5572 1070L5490 1016"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5562 1098h0M5552 978h0M5549 1060h0M53